caption: Numbering the records
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes/number-records
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

`@counter` is the record's position in the run, counting from 1 like
the `$list` widget's counter.  Padded, it sorts:

```
"tw-fields": {
  "title": "Card {{@counter|zero-pad[3]}}"
}
```

gives `Card 001`, `Card 002`, …  When the data has its own identifier,
pad that instead — `{{unique_id|zero-pad[4]}}` — and keep `@counter`
for a batch position or a tie-breaker:

```
"custom-fields": {
  "batch-order": "{{@counter}}",
  "id":          "{{unique_id|zero-pad[4]}}"
}
```

The counter restarts at 1 on every ''Convert'', so it is a position
within one import, not an identity across imports.
